    "body": "If you haven’t already, check out our [contributing guidelines](https://github.com/Expensify/ReactNativeChat/blob/main/contributingGuides/CONTRIBUTING.md) for onboarding. To join our Slack channel, fill out [this form](https://forms.gle/Q7hnhUJPnQCK7Fe56).\n___\n\n**Version Number:** 9.5.1-9\n**Reproducible in staging?:** Yes\n**Reproducible in production?:** Yes\n**If this was caught during regression testing, add the test name, ID and link from BrowserStack:** https://github.com/Expensify/App/pull/102699\n**Email or phone of affected tester (no customers):** N/A\n**Issue reported by:** Applause Internal Team\n**Bug source:** Pull Request QA execution\n**Device used:** Windows 11 / Chrome, Android 16 / Samsung Galaxy A06\n**App Component:** Workspace Settings\n\n## Action Performed:\nPrecondition: a workspace on the Control plan whose owner and admin are not in the vendorMatching beta, connected to Xero with the sync finished, holding at least one non-reimbursable (company card) expense.\n1. Sign in to staging.new.expensify.com as the workspace admin\n2. Open a non-reimbursable expense\n3. Tap the Supplier row, pick a supplier\n4. Log in to https://go.xero.com/AccountsReceivable/Search.aspx\n5. Go to Contacts > Suppliers and open the supplier you picked \n6. Click Options (three vertical dots, top right of the page) and choose Archive, then confirm\n7. Back in Expensify, Sync the Xero connection\n8. Reopen the expense from step 3\n\n## Expected Result:\nThe Supplier row should now show a Supplier no longer valid violation\n\n## Actual Result:\nThe Supplier shows a Vendor no longer valid violation\n\n## Workaround:\nUnknown\n\n## Platforms:\n- [x] Android: App\n- [ ] Android: mWeb Chrome\n- [ ] iOS: App\n- [ ] iOS: mWeb Safari\n- [ ] iOS: mWeb Chrome\n- [x] Windows: Chrome\n- [ ] MacOS: Chrome Safari\n\n## Screenshots/Videos\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4985f86e-50b5-4fc1-b027-635234d2620b\n\n[View all open jobs on GitHub](https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues?q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Help+Wanted%22)\n\n\n> **Applause Internal Information**\n> Exported by: Julia Ponikarchuk\n> Bug ID: 7276050\n<details><summary>Upwork Automation - Do Not Edit</summary>\n    <ul>\n        <li>Upwork Job URL: <a href=\"https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022106793766897454925\">https://www.upwork.com/jobs/~022106793766897454925</a></li>\n        <li>Upwork Job ID: 2106793766897454925</li>\n        <li>Last Price Increase: 2026-10-04</li>\n    </ul>\n</details>",
