      "body": "<details><summary>Proposal</summary>\n\n### Please re-state the problem that we are trying to solve in this issue.\nOn a workspace with Xero integration enabled and vendor matching active, when an assigned supplier contact is archived in Xero and the workspace is synced, reopening the expense incorrectly displays \"Vendor no longer valid\" on the Supplier row instead of \"Supplier no longer valid\".\n\n### What is the root cause of that problem?\nIn `src/libs/Violations/ViolationsUtils.ts` (lines 605–630), reconciliation logic was implemented to ensure `inactiveVendor` violations receive `data.isSupplierViolation: true` when Xero is the active matching source (`isXeroActiveMatchingSource(policy)`). \n\nHowever, this reconciliation is located inside `compareAndSetViolations()`, which only executes when an expense transaction is actively updated or edited. When a user merely reopens or views an existing expense following a backend Xero sync, `compareAndSetViolations()` does not run.\n\nInstead, the UI components (`MoneyRequestView`, `TransactionPreviewContent`, `ReportActionItem`, etc.) read the stored violation directly from Onyx and pass it to `ViolationsUtils.getViolationTranslation()`:\nhttps://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/main/src/libs/Violations/ViolationsUtils.ts#L991-L1032\n\nIn `getViolationTranslation()`:\n```typescript\nconst {\n    isSupplierViolation = false,\n} = violation.data ?? {};\n\nswitch (violation.name) {\n    case 'inactiveVendor':\n        return translate('violations.inactiveVendor', isSupplierViolation);\n```\nBecause the server-generated violation created during the Xero sync arrives without `violation.data.isSupplierViolation`, it defaults to `false`. As a result, `translate('violations.inactiveVendor', false)` is returned, which renders the fallback copy `\"Vendor no longer valid\"` rather than `\"Supplier no longer valid\"`.\n\n### What changes do you think we should make in order to solve the problem?\n1. In `src/libs/Violations/ViolationsUtils.ts`:\n   Extend `ViolationTranslationParams` to accept an optional `isSupplier?: boolean`:\n   ```typescript\n   type ViolationTranslationParams = {\n       // ... existing properties\n       isSupplier?: boolean;\n   };\n   ```\n   In `getViolationTranslation()`, update the `inactiveVendor` branch to prefer `params.isSupplier` when provided, falling back to `violation.data?.isSupplierViolation`:\n   ```typescript\n   case CONST.VIOLATIONS.INACTIVE_VENDOR: {\n       const isSupplier = params.isSupplier ?? isSupplierViolation;\n       return translate('violations.inactiveVendor', isSupplier);\n   }\n   ```\n   This guarantees that:\n   - When policy context is present at render time, the active matching source (`isXeroActiveMatchingSource(policy)`) authoritatively governs the terminology.\n   - If an integration changes back from Xero to QBO/Intacct, `isSupplier: false` correctly overrides any stale `isSupplierViolation: true` flag.\n   - If no policy context is available, it gracefully preserves the stored `data.isSupplierViolation` fallback.\n\n2. In the components that render transaction violations for an expense (`MoneyRequestView`, `TransactionPreviewContent`, `ReportActionItem`, and RBR message formatters `getRBRMessages` / `TransactionItemRowRBR`):\n   Derive `isSupplier` from the already-subscribed `policy` entry in Onyx using `PolicyUtils.isXeroActiveMatchingSource(policy)` and pass it into `getViolationTranslation`:\n   ```typescript\n   const isSupplier = PolicyUtils.isXeroActiveMatchingSource(policy);\n   // passed in params: { ...params, isSupplier }\n   ```\n\n3. **Automated Unit Tests:**\n   Add comprehensive test coverage in `tests/unit/ViolationsUtilsTest.ts`:\n   - Verify `getViolationTranslation` with `inactiveVendor` and `isSupplier: true` returns `\"Supplier no longer valid\"`.\n   - Verify `getViolationTranslation` with `inactiveVendor` and `isSupplier: false` (with stale `data.isSupplierViolation: true`) returns `\"Vendor no longer valid\"`.\n   - Verify fallback behavior when `params.isSupplier` is omitted.\n\n### What alternative solutions did you explore? (Optional)\n- Forcing `compareAndSetViolations()` on expense mount/reopen: Rejected because running reconciliation mutations on read-only view operations causes unnecessary writes to Onyx and re-renders.\n- Relying solely on `data.isSupplierViolation`: Rejected because server-synced violations from Xero sync do not include this client-specific presentation flag.\n</details>\n\nContributor details\nYour Expensify account email: camesenin@gmail.com\nUpwork Profile Link: https://www.upwork.com/freelancers/~0170d6b02e9440e604\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
