      "body": "## Proposal\n\n### What is the root cause of that problem?\n\nThe violation text picks \"Supplier\" or \"Vendor\" from a flag stored on the violation (`data.isSupplierViolation`). It defaults to \"Vendor\" when the flag is missing ([`ViolationsUtils.ts:992`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/f4c2005cd2dfac6b0ac282ce0a0bdb9484cac53f/src/libs/Violations/ViolationsUtils.ts#L992), [`:1031-1032`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/f4c2005cd2dfac6b0ac282ce0a0bdb9484cac53f/src/libs/Violations/ViolationsUtils.ts#L1031-L1032)).\n\nIn this flow, the backend adds the `inactiveVendor` violation during the Xero sync, and that violation has no flag. The app only adds the flag when it recalculates violations locally ([`ViolationsUtils.ts:606-630`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/f4c2005cd2dfac6b0ac282ce0a0bdb9484cac53f/src/libs/Violations/ViolationsUtils.ts#L606-L630)), which happens only when the expense is edited. Reopening the expense doesn't recalculate, so the row shows \"Vendor no longer valid\".\n\nThe row label itself is correct because it checks the workspace each time it renders ([`MoneyRequestView.tsx:588`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/f4c2005cd2dfac6b0ac282ce0a0bdb9484cac53f/src/components/ReportActionItem/MoneyRequestView.tsx#L588)).\n\n### What changes do you think we should make in order to solve the problem?\n\nChoose the wording when the message renders, using the same workspace check as the row label. Don't rely only on the stored flag.\n\n1. Add an optional `isSupplier` param to `ViolationTranslationParams` and `getViolationTranslation`. For `inactiveVendor`, use `isSupplierViolation || isSupplier`.\n2. Pass `isSupplier: isXeroActiveMatchingSource(policy)` from each caller that has the policy: `MoneyRequestView`, `MoneyRequestReceiptView`, `ViolationMessages`, and `TransactionPreviewContent`.\n3. Add a test: a violation with no flag, rendered on a Xero-active workspace, returns \"Supplier no longer valid\".\n\n### What alternative solutions did you explore? (Optional)\n\n- Have the backend set `isSupplierViolation` when it creates the violation for Xero. That fix belongs outside the App repo, and older stored violations would still need the render-time fix.\n- Recalculate violations when the expense opens. This adds work to every expense view just to fix one label.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Investigation details</summary>\n\n- A unit test already describes this case: \"The backend can fire `inactiveVendor` directly (e.g. after a supplier deletion + sync) — that violation has no `data.isSupplierViolation` flag\" ([`ViolationUtilsTest.ts:3517-3521`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/f4c2005cd2dfac6b0ac282ce0a0bdb9484cac53f/tests/unit/ViolationUtilsTest.ts#L3517-L3521)). That backfill covers only local recalculation, not the view-only path in this report.\n- `MoneyRequestView` calls `getViolationTranslation` without any policy context ([`MoneyRequestView.tsx:867-879`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/f4c2005cd2dfac6b0ac282ce0a0bdb9484cac53f/src/components/ReportActionItem/MoneyRequestView.tsx#L867-L879)).\n- [Remove the vendorMatching beta gate from Xero flows](https://github.com/Expensify/App/pull/102699) didn't create this bug. It made the Supplier row visible to users outside the beta, so more people now see it.\n- Out of scope: the parameter-free Search column label `violations.shortName.inactiveVendor` is hardcoded to \"Vendor no longer valid\" ([`en.ts:11029`](https://github.com/Expensify/App/blob/f4c2005cd2dfac6b0ac282ce0a0bdb9484cac53f/src/languages/en.ts#L11029)).\n- This wasn't reproduced live because the test environment has no Xero connection. The analysis is based on the code.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n**Next Steps for Contributor+ team:**\n**To accept:** `@MelvinBot implement [this](https://github.com/Expensify/App/issues/102943)` to create a draft PR.\n**To refine:** `@MelvinBot <your feedback>`\n**To reject:** Explain why you are rejecting Melvin's proposal.\n\n\n---\n_[view run](https://github.com/Expensify/melvin/actions/runs/37219111802)_\n",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
